  "text": "←\nAll states\nStatewide sales tax\nNone\nStatus\nNo general sales tax\nWhat's taxed?\nGood to know\nCommon questions\nHere's how each kind of item is treated in this state. Tap a row to read the plain-English note.\nWhat you're buying\nSales tax?\nWhat that means\nBullion Bars\nNo sales tax\nNo sales tax in Oregon. You won't see sales tax on this on your order.\nBullion Coins\nNo sales tax\nNo sales tax in Oregon. You won't see sales tax on this on your order.\nBullion Rounds\nNo sales tax\nNo sales tax in Oregon. You won't see sales tax on this on your order.\nLegal-Tender Coins\nNo sales tax\nNo sales tax in Oregon. You won't see sales tax on this on your order.\nNumismatic Coins\nNo sales tax\nNo sales tax in Oregon. You won't see sales tax on this on your order.\nJewelry\nNo sales tax\nNo sales tax in Oregon. You won't see sales tax on this on your order.\nIndustrial Precious Metal\nNo sales tax\nNo sales tax in Oregon. You won't see sales tax on this on your order.\nCollectibles (Non-Coin)\nNo sales tax\nNo sales tax in Oregon. You won't see sales tax on this on your order.\nPaper Currency\nNo sales tax\nNo sales tax in Oregon. You won't see sales tax on this on your order.\nAccessories\nNo sales tax\nNo sales tax in Oregon. You won't see sales tax on this on your order.\nWhat's covered by the exemption\nOregon has no general sales tax — there is nothing to exempt or apply.\nWhat's NOT covered\nNo general sales tax\nCommon questions about sales tax on gold and silver in Oregon.\nIs gold bullion taxed in Oregon?\n+\nNo. Oregon has no state sales tax, so you do not pay Oregon sales tax on gold bullion purchases.\nAre silver coins subject to sales tax in Oregon?\n+\nNo. With no general Oregon sales tax, silver coins are not charged sales tax at checkout.\nDo I owe sales tax on jewelry in Oregon?\n+\nNo. Oregon does not impose a general state sales tax, so jewelry is not subject to Oregon sales tax.",
